# clangd config for fb-sim. There is no compile_commands.json (the build is a handful of Makefile
# recipes, not a generator-based build system) and the individual recipes even mix -std=c++17 object
# files with a -std=c++20 GPU/webgpu translation unit (render/, render/stages/, world/World.cpp,
# clients/) inside the SAME native/wasm target -- see sim/Makefile. C++20 is a safe superset of the C++17
# subset used here (no `concept`/`requires`/`co_*`/`char8_t` identifiers in the c++17-only TUs, checked
# via grep), so one shared std/include profile below is accurate for every file and far less fragile
# than PathMatch-splitting by directory (a new .cpp landing in the wrong subtree would silently fall
# outside a narrower rule).
#
# Paths are ABSOLUTE, not sim-relative: with no compilation database, clangd's synthetic fallback
# compile command resolves each file's OWN directory as the base for relative -I/-isystem flags (proven
# by `clangd --check` -- e.g. src/render/stages/TilesStage.cpp got `-Isrc/core` resolved against
# .../sim/src/render/stages, not sim/), so sim-relative flags silently miss for anything outside sim/'s
# own top level. Absolute paths sidestep that without needing a generated compile_commands.json (more
# moving parts -- a generation script to keep in sync with the Makefile's per-TU std/-I mix -- for the
# same maintenance burden of updating roots when the Makefile's -I list changes).
#
# Include roots mirror sim/Makefile's INC_MODULES/INC_NATIVE/INC_CLIENT + INC_TILES (../tiles/src,
# style_ver.h -- world/TerrainLoader.cpp's one cross-project reference) + the native recipe's vendor
# isystem set (Dawn generated + vendored webgpu_cpp.h, the curl compat shim) -- update alongside the
# Makefile if either changes.
#
# Out of scope: src/clients/AppWasm.cpp, world/TerrainLoader.cpp and world/TilePool.cpp
# #include <emscripten.h>. Pointing
# clangd at emsdk's own sysroot fights its libc++-vs-libc header ordering when driven by plain clang
# instead of em++ (tried; made things worse) -- reproducing that needs em++ itself as the compile
# driver (an emcc-generated compile_commands.json), a bigger lift outside this file's reported bug.
CompileFlags:
  Add:
    - -std=c++20
    - -Wall
    - -Wextra
    - -Wpedantic
    - -Wno-unused-parameter
    - -I/Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/sim/src/core
    - -I/Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/sim/src/render
    - -I/Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/sim/src/world
    - -I/Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/sim/src/world/terrain
    - -I/Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/sim/src/clients
    - -I/Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/tiles/src
    - -isystem
    - /Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/sim/vendor/dawn/out/gen/include
    - -isystem
    - /Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/sim/vendor/dawn/include
    - -isystem
    - /Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/sim/vendor
    - -isystem
    - /Users/cosmo/Git/flightbox/sim/vendor/.compat-headers
